One thing BIL can't automatically do for you is decide when certain animations or variants should be used. To do this, every holder provides an Animator and VariantController, which can for example be used like this: Animator animator = holder.getAnimator(); // Completely stops the animation named 'idle'.
animator.stopAnimation("idle"); // Pauses the animation named 'walk'.
animator.pauseAnimation("walk"); // Plays the melee animation with priority 10.
animator.playAnimation("melee", 10); VariantController controller = holder.getVariantController(); // Sets the variant to the variant named 'hurt' if the current variant is default.
if (controller.isDefaultVariant()) { controller.setVariant("hurt");
}

